I tend to agree.  I feel a luckstone doesn't push you towards victory
nearly as well as say speed boots or gray dragon scale mail, but there
are times when it is a good wish.

spoilers

Luck can get you the Mjollnir you seek, save you from certain death, and
give you all sorts of other goodies in addition to helping you hit monsters
in combat.

Many of the benefits of high luck are realized through prayer.  However,
if you allow your luck to get high enough, a "bad" thing can happen when you
pray:  You could get crowned Hand of Elbereth/Arioch.  While it does give
you lots of spiffy intrinsics, it increases the amount of time you have to
wait before you can pray successfully.
